course: dictionary
lesson: 10784
title: Grand words for brave heroes
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Valorous means very brave, especially in battle. It is a grand, old-fashioned word, so you will mostly find it in storybooks and old tales, not in everyday talk.
explain: Look for clues in the word itself. Valour means bravery, so valorous is the word for someone full of valour. A «valorous knight» is a knight who is very brave.
explain: Read the example: «Here and there wicked little faces popped out of holes, but vanished immediately at sight of the valorous animal, his pistols, and the great ugly cudgel in his grasp». The wicked faces vanish when they see him, so the animal must be brave. To check, swap in brave: the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Valorous means very brave, especially in battle.
fact: Valour means bravery, and valorous comes from it.
fact: «A valorous knight» means a brave knight.
fact: Valorous is a formal, old word, so it often appears in old stories and poems.
fact: Toad in The Wind in the Willows likes to think of himself as valorous.
exercise: «A valorous knight rode out to save the village.» What does valorous mean? | Very tired from riding | Very quiet | Very kind to animals | *Very brave
exercise: «Her valour during the storm saved the crew.» Find and copy the word from the same family as valorous, which means bravery. | *valour | storm | during | crew
exercise: Toad likes to think of himself as valorous. What does he like to think he is? | Very old | Very quiet and shy | Very hungry | *Very brave
test: «The valorous firefighters ran into the burning house.» What does valorous mean here? | *Very brave | Very slow | Very wet | Very sleepy
test: Dana reads «a valorous queen». Which word could replace valorous and keep the meaning close? | Hungry | Lazy | *Brave | Gentle
exam: What does valorous mean? | *Very brave, especially in battle | Very hungry | Very old and worn out | Very quiet and gentle
